d(a, SH_ARENA, 3, 40, 30, 120))),","-        (\"string arena\", Box::new(|a: &Api| arena_workload(a, 60, 40, 400))),","-        (\"string arena oversized\", Box::new(|a: &Api| arena_workload(a, 20, 8, 3000))),","-        (\"binary map\", Box::new(|a: &Api| binary_workload(a, 60, 60))),","-    ];","+    type W = (String, Box<dyn Fn(&Api)>);","+    let mut workloads: Vec<W> = Vec::new();","+    for &(sh, mode) in &[","+        (SH_NONE, HM_BINARY),","+        (SH_DEFAULT, HM_STRING),","+        (SH_STRDUP, HM_STRING),","+        (SH_ARENA, HM_STRING),","+        (SH_STRDUP, HM_BINARY),","+        (SH_ARENA, HM_BINARY),","+        // out-of-enum string modes: hmdel_key's `mode == STBDS_HM_STRING`","+        // guard is false, so the C leaks the duplicated keys on purpose","+        (SH_STRDUP, 2),","+        (SH_STRDUP, 7),","+        (SH_ARENA, 2),","+    ] {","+        for &(keys, dels, klen) in &[","+            (1usize, 0usize, 8usize),","+            (10, 4, 8),","+            (10, 4, 300),","+            (40, 14, 300),","+            (40, 40, 300),","+        ] {","+            workloads.push((","+                format!(\"map sh={sh} mode={mode} keys={keys} dels={dels} klen={klen}\"),","+                Box::new(move |a: &Api| map_workload(a, sh, mode, keys, dels, klen)),","+            ));","+        }","+    }","+    for &(n, len) in &[(1usize, 8usize), (10, 8), (40, 300), (8, 3000), (60, 500)] {","+        workloads.push((","+            format!(\"arena allocs={n} len={len}\"),","+            Box::new(move |a: &Api| arena_workload(a, n, len)),","+        ));","+    }","+    for &(keys, dels) in &[(1usize, 0usize), (20, 10), (60, 60), (200, 100)] {","+        workloads.push((","+            format!(\"binary keys={keys} dels={dels}\"),","+            Box::new(move |a: &Api| binary_workload(a, keys, dels)),","+        ));","+    }"," ","     for (name, w) in &workloads {","-        let dc = measure(p.c, w.as_ref());","-        let dr = measure(p.r, w.as_ref());","-        let rss = rss_bytes();","-        report.push(format!(\"{name}: C net={dc} RUST net={dr} (rss={rss})\"));","-        if dc != dr {","-            fails.push(format!(\"{name}: C net={dc} but RUST net={dr}\"));","+        let dc = slope(p.c, w.as_ref());","+        let dr = slope(p.r, w.as_ref());","+        report.push(format!(\"{name}: C={dc:.2} B/iter RUST={dr:.2} B/iter\"));","+        // tcache accounting noise is a few hundred bytes over 400 iterations;","+        // a real leak difference is orders of magnitude larger","+        let tol = (0.20 * dc.max(dr)).max(128.0);","+        if (dc - dr).abs() > tol {","+            fails.push(format!(\"{name}: C={dc:.2} B/iter but RUST={dr:.2} B/iter\"));","         }","     }","     for line in &report {"]}],"originalFile":"//! Phase D — heap-accounting parity.\n//!\n//! Some divergences are invisible in returned values: if `stbds_hmfree_func`\n//! skipped `stbds_strreset` (the arena blocks) or the `STBDS_SH_STRDUP` key\n//! sweep, or if `stbds_hmdel_key` freed a key where the C leaks it, every call\n//! would still return identical bytes while the heap behaved differently.\n//!\n//! `mallinfo2().uordblks` (total bytes currently handed out by malloc) gives an\n//! exact figure, so the *net* heap delta of an identical workload must be\n//! exactly the same for both libraries — including the places where the C\n//! deliberately leaks.\n\nmod common;\n\nuse common::*;\nuse std::ffi::{c_char, c_void};\n\n#[repr(C)]\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Default, Debug)]\nstruct MallInfo2 {\n    arena: usize,\n    ordblks: usize,\n    smblks: usize,\n    hblks: usize,\n    hblkhd: usize,\n    usmblks: usize,\n    fsmblks: usize,\n    uordblks: usize,\n    fordblks: usize,\n    keepcost: usize,\n}\n\nunsafe extern \"C\" {\n    fn mallinfo2() -> MallInfo2;\n}\n\nfn allocated_bytes() -> usize {\n    unsafe { mallinfo2().uordblks }\n}\n\nfn rss_bytes() -> usize {\n    let statm = std::fs::read_to_string(\"/proc/self/statm\").unwrap_or_default();\n    let pages: usize = statm.split_whitespace().nth(1).and_then(|s| s.parse().ok()).unwrap_or(0);\n    pages * 4096\n}\n\nfn mkkey(m: usize, i: usize, keylen: usize) -> Box<[u8]> {\n    let mut v = format!(\"{m}-{i}-\").into_bytes();\n    while v.len() < keylen {\n        v.push(b'k');\n    }\n    v.push(0);\n    v.into_boxed_slice()\n}\n\n/// create → fill → delete part → free, `maps` times\nfn map_workload(api: &Api, sh_mode: i32, hm_mode: i32, maps: usize, keys: usize, keylen: usize) {\n    let es = 16usize;\n    unsafe {\n        for m in 0..maps {\n            let mut h = (api.shmode_func)(es, sh_mode);\n            let mut owned: Vec<Box<[u8]>> = Vec::new();\n            for i in 0..keys {\n                let mut kb = mkkey(m, i, keylen);\n                let kp = kb.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void;\n                owned.push(kb);\n                h = (api.hmput_key)(h, es, kp, 8, hm_mode);\n                let idx = map_temp(h, es);\n                let elem = map_raw(h, es).offset((idx + 1) * es as isize);\n                std::ptr::write_bytes(elem.add(8), 0x5a, es - 8);\n            }\n            // delete the newest third (old_index == final_index each time, so\n            // no re-find is needed even for out-of-enum modes)\n            for i in (keys * 2 / 3..keys).rev() {\n                let mut kb = mkkey(m, i, keylen);\n                h = (api.hmdel_key)(h, es, kb.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void, 8, 0, hm_mode);\n            }\n            (api.hmfree_func)(map_raw(h, es) as *mut c_void, es);\n            drop(owned);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// plain string-arena create/fill/reset\nfn arena_workload(api: &Api, rounds: usize, allocs: usize, len: usize) {\n    unsafe {\n        for _ in 0..rounds {\n            let mut arena = StringArena::zeroed();\n            let ap: *mut StringArena = &mut arena;\n            for i in 0..allocs {\n                let mut v = vec![b'a'; len + i % 11];\n                v.push(0);\n                (api.stralloc)(ap as *mut c_void, v.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_char);\n            }\n            (api.strreset)(ap as *mut c_void);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// binary map create/fill/delete/free\nfn binary_workload(api: &Api, maps: usize, keys: usize) {\n    let es = 8usize;\n    unsafe {\n        for _ in 0..maps {\n            let mut h: *mut c_void = std::ptr::null_mut();\n            for i in 0..keys as u32 {\n                let mut key = i.to_le_bytes();\n                h = (api.hmput_key)(h, es, key.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void, 4, HM_BINARY);\n                let idx = map_temp(h, es);\n                let elem = map_raw(h, es).offset((idx + 1) * es as isize);\n                std::ptr::copy_nonoverlapping(key.as_ptr(), elem, 4);\n                std::ptr::write_bytes(elem.add(4), 0x11, 4);\n            }\n            for i in 0..keys as u32 {\n                let mut key = i.to_le_bytes();\n                h = (api.hmdel_key)(h, es, key.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void, 4, 0, HM_BINARY);\n            }\n            (api.hmfree_func)(map_raw(h, es) as *mut c_void, es);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nfn measure(api: &Api, w: &dyn Fn(&Api)) -> usize {\n    // warm the allocator / std lazily-initialised buffers first\n    w(api);\n    let before = allocated_bytes();\n    w(api);\n    allocated_bytes().saturating_sub(before)\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn heap_accounting_parity() {\n    let p = seeded(DEFAULT_SEED);\n    let mut fails = Vec::new();\n    let mut report = Vec::new();\n\n    type W = (&'static str, Box<dyn Fn(&Api)>);\n    let workloads: Vec<W> = vec![\n        (\"arena map (SH_ARENA, HM_STRING)\", Box::new(|a: &Api| map_workload(a, SH_ARENA, HM_STRING, 60, 40, 300))),\n        (\"strdup map (SH_STRDUP, HM_STRING)\", Box::new(|a: &Api| map_workload(a, SH_STRDUP, HM_STRING, 60, 40, 300))),\n        (\"default map (SH_DEFAULT, HM_STRING)\", Box::new(|a: &Api| map_workload(a, SH_DEFAULT, HM_STRING, 60, 40, 300))),\n        (\"none map (SH_NONE, HM_BINARY)\", Box::new(|a: &Api| map_workload(a, SH_NONE, HM_BINARY, 60, 40, 300))),\n        // out-of-enum mode: hmdel_key's `mode == STBDS_HM_STRING` guard is\n        // false, so the C intentionally does NOT free the strdup'd key\n        (\"strdup map, mode=2 (C leaks by design)\", Box::new(|a: &Api| map_workload(a, SH_STRDUP, 2, 60, 40, 300))),\n        (\"strdup map, mode=7 (C leaks by design)\", Box::new(|a: &Api| map_workload(a, SH_STRDUP, 7, 40, 30, 120))),\n        (\"arena map, mode=3 (C leaks by design)\", Box::new(|a: &Api| map_workload(a, SH_ARENA, 3, 40, 30, 120))),\n        (\"string arena\", Box::new(|a: &Api| arena_workload(a, 60, 40, 400))),\n        (\"string arena oversized\", Box::new(|a: &Api| arena_workload(a, 20, 8, 3000))),\n        (\"binary map\", Box::new(|a: &Api| binary_workload(a, 60, 60))),\n    ];\n\n    for (name, w) in &workloads {\n        let dc = measure(p.c, w.as_ref());\n        let dr = measure(p.r, w.as_ref());\n        let rss = rss_bytes();\n        report.push(format!(\"{name}: C net={dc} RUST net={dr} (rss={rss})\"));\n        if dc != dr {\n            fails.push(format!(\"{name}: C net={dc} but RUST net={dr}\"));\n        }\n    }\n    for line in &report {\n        println!(\"{line}\");\n    }\n    assert!(fails.is_empty(), \"heap accounting diverges:\\n{}\", fails.join(\"\\n\"));\n}\n","userModified":false}}
