{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_cq3qhdftgppmji65vpi74tz4zy77lgjbstqwpx2c2kdc7j6xoevq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. Here's the final report.\n\n## Result: the translation is byte-faithful — no fixes were required\n\n`translation/src/lib.rs` is **unmodified** (md5 identical to the baseline I took before testing). Every divergence I chased turned out to be either a flaw in my measurement or an intentional C quirk that the Rust already reproduced.\n\n### Phase A — surface mapped (artifacts in `translation/`)\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | all 16 `nm -D` symbols; C↔Rust name sets `diff` **empty**; imports are libc/Rust-runtime only |\n| `ERRORS.md` | **43 rows**, one per distinct rejection in `lib.c` (every `return -1`/`NULL`/`temp=0` sentinel, all 8 `STBDS_ASSERT`s, mode/enum guards, arena min/max constants) + row→test mapping |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | **53 rows** over the real branch axes: `mode` (`HM_*`, incl. out-of-enum), `string.mode` (all 4 `SH_*`), creation route, seed, `keyoffset` × input shapes (`elemsize` 1…64, `keysize` 0…16, counts 0/1/5/**6**/7/…/1000, delete position/volume, string lengths 0…3000) |\n| `MUTATIONS.md` | sensitivity evidence (below) |\n\n### Phases B/C/D — 80 differential tests, both `.so`s loaded via `libloading`\nNothing calls Rust directly; both libraries are loaded by path and driven through the low-level `stbds_hm*_key` entry points, not just wrappers. After **every single call**, both sides are compared on a full structural snapshot: array header (`length`/`capacity`/`temp`), all live element bytes (`char*` keys compared by pointee string), and the entire `stbds_hash_index` including every `hash[8]`/`index[8]` bucket — plus pointer-identity relations only where C guarantees them.\n\nThree real issues surfaced, all in *my* harness, and each taught something worth recording:\n- `realloc` may or may not move a block → identity is only comparable when capacity is unchanged.\n- Uninitialised payload bytes are uninitialised heap → the runner now always fills the value region.\n- `mallinfo2().uordblks` counts tcache-held chunks as in-use → the \"C leaks 2224 B\" signal was noise; a 400-iteration **slope** shows 0 B/iter for both, and identical leak rates (e.g. 12800 B/iter) in the configurations where the C leaks *on purpose* (`hmdel_key` frees the duplicated key only when `mode == STBDS_HM_STRING` **exactly**).\n\nQuirks explicitly pinned down as preserved: siphash's C integer-promotion sign extension, `hash ^= hash ^ X`, `temp_key` written in the first probe loop but left **stale** in the wrap-around loop, `arrgrowf(NULL,es,0,0) → NULL`, `(unsigned char)` truncation of out-of-enum `SH_*` modes, and the dead `v32` argument of `stbds_load_32_or_64`.\n\n### Mutation study — 48 injected bugs, 43 caught\nThe 5 survivors are **provably equivalent** mutants (`free(NULL)` on the always-NULL default slot; the dead `v32` argument; a bucket-array alignment that changes only an address; `min_cap = min_len` when they're equal; re-scanning bucket slots the first probe loop already rejected).\n\n### Completion gate\n- [x] `SYMBOLS.md`: 16/16 symbols, 0 missing, 0 undefined non-libc symbols\n- [x] Phase B: all **53** `CONFIGS.md` rows pass across seeded randomized inputs\n- [x] Phase C: all **43** `ERRORS.md` rows have a passing differential test (37 executed directly; 6 are documented-unreachable/abort-only, e.g. `arrfreef(NULL)`)\n- [x] Holds under **every** configuration: `default` and `--no-default-features` (Cargo.toml declares no `[features]`), in both `release` (`overflow-checks = false`) and `dev` profiles → `scratch/run_all.sh` prints `ALL GREEN`\n\nOne operational gotcha worth knowing: `cargo test` does **not** rebuild a `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` artifact, so `run_all.sh` always runs `cargo build` first — otherwise the tests silently load a stale `.so`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1994,"cache_read_input_tokens":325601,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1994,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ece1fe0a-8825-4840-af0e-a0dc99e742ce","uuid":"5b9cda30-6792-4acf-9186-d808c8cf68d0","timestamp":"2026-08-27T11:55:48.126Z"}
